sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Caller as a scenario<br/>internal/command/middleware/unitofwork/test/nested_steps_test.go
    participant Middleware as commandunitofwork.Middleware<br/>internal/command/middleware/unitofwork/unitofwork.go
    participant Import as ImportItemsHandler<br/>internal/command/import_items.go
    participant Add as AddItemHandler<br/>internal/command/add_item.go
    participant Repository as postgres.Repository of ItemRow<br/>internal/infrastructure/postgres/repository.go
    participant Unit as the GORM plugin<br/>internal/infrastructure/postgres/unitofwork/unitofwork.go
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Caller->>+Middleware: Handlers.ImportItems.Handle(ctx, ImportItemsCommand)
    Middleware->>Unit: Begin(ctx): a new unit in ctx, true, this command ends it
    Middleware->>+Import: next(ctx)
    loop one nested AddItemCommand per title, through the decorated AddItem
        Import->>+Add: Handle(ctx): the middleware calls Begin, false, and passes on
        Add->>+Repository: Insert(ctx, &ItemRow), through service.ItemLists
        Repository->>+Unit: the callback before the write
        Note over Unit,DB: the first write takes a connection and BEGIN, each write has a SAVEPOINT
        Unit-->>-Repository: the statement runs in the unit's transaction
        Repository->>+DB: INSERT
        DB-->>-Repository: the row, or 23505: ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
        Repository-->>-Add: nil, or ErrDuplicateKey told as a conflict
        Add-->>-Import: result, or the conflict
    end
    Import-->>-Middleware: result, or the conflict
    alt the handler returned
        Middleware->>+Unit: Commit(context.WithoutCancel(ctx))
        Unit->>DB: COMMIT
        Unit-->>-Middleware: nil, or a failure told as unavailable
    else the handler failed
        Middleware->>+Unit: Rollback(context.WithoutCancel(ctx))
        Unit->>DB: ROLLBACK
        Unit-->>-Middleware: done
    end
    Middleware-->>-Caller: the result, or the failure
